(62, $t$No school-specific supplemental essay. An open-topic essay (Common App/SUNY App essay) is required. However, Honors College, WISE, and University Scholars require a ~250-word program-fit statement; Scholars for Medicine/Dental Medicine require an additional essay of 650 words or fewer; Creative Writing majors need a writing sample.$t$, null, $t$Presidential Scholarships; Honors College Scholarships; Valedictorian and Salutatorian Scholarships; National Merit Scholarships; WISE; Regeneron STS Scholarships (automatic review of admitted first-years); Global Excellence Scholarship and #YouAreWelcomeHere (50% tuition) for international first-years$t$),
(63, $t$Essay not required — no supplemental essay. Per the official checklist, only the application, application fee, and self-reported academic record are required, and the Common App's official guidance also states 'No essays, letters of recommendation, ACT/SAT scores, or official transcripts are required to apply'. Short-response questions within the application are optional and used for review and scholarship consideration.$t$, null, $t$Global Excellence Scholarship (international F-1 freshmen, $5,000-$20,000/yr for 4 yrs, automatic consideration, notified by end of March); U of M Gold Scholar Award (up to $10,000/yr, preference to National Merit Finalists naming UMN first choice); university-wide academic scholarships (automatic consideration, some need-based)$t$),
(64, $t$No required supplemental essay. Optionally, 1 academic writing sample (a school assignment, graded or ungraded) may be submitted — not an essay prompt.$t$, null, $t$Official international financial aid page: "Although Williams isn't need-blind for international applicants, approximately 70% of international students receive financial aid from the college, with aid awards averaging more than $90,000 annually... Financial aid awards for international students are comprehensive, meet 100% of demonstrated need and are guaranteed for all four years." All-Grant program: "loans will never be included in your financial aid award from Williams." There are no merit scholarships (CDS H6: only need-based aid offered to nonresidents); all aid is need-based. International students must indicate their intent to apply for financial aid on the admission application.$t$),
